/target
/downloads/
# Local working notes; never committed.
/local/
# Never commit any SWF, wherever it sits: they are the original game's code and art.
# One pattern for every capitalisation: .gitignore is case-sensitive on Linux, and a `.SWF`
# or `.Swf` file from a Windows machine would slip past `*.swf` there.
*.[sS][wW][fF]
# Generated by build.rs (cargo-about) and by the release job; not source.
/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES
# The original's launcher (Isaac.exe wraps the SWF) and any build output for Windows are binaries;
# release builds come from CI, never from the repository. Same capitalisation trick as above.
*.[eE][xX][eE]
# IDE project files (JetBrains).
/.idea/
# Screenshots show the original's art (the game's own pictures), so they stay local.
/screenshots/
# The assistant's local settings and hooks.
/.claude/
__pycache__/
